1b[1G\u001b[J◓  Waiting for agent reply…\u001b[1G\u001b[J◑  Waiting for agent reply…\u001b[1G\u001b[J◒  Waiting for agent reply…\u001b[1G\u001b[J◐  Waiting for agent reply…\u001b[1G\u001b[J◓  Waiting for agent reply…\u001b[1G\u001b[J◑  Waiting for agent reply…\u001b[1G\u001b[J◒  Waiting for agent reply…\u001b[1G\u001b[J◐  Waiting for agent reply….\u001b[1G\u001b[J◓  Waiting for agent reply….\u001b[1G\u001b[J◑  Waiting for agent reply….\u001b[1G\u001b[J◒  Waiting for agent reply….\u001b[1G\u001b[J◐  Waiting for agent reply….\u001b[1G\u001b[J◓  Waiting for agent reply….\u001b[1G\u001b[J◑  Waiting for agent reply….\u001b[1G\u001b[J◒  Waiting for agent reply….\u001b[1G\u001b[J◐  Waiting for agent reply…..\u001b[1G\u001b[J◓  Waiting for agent reply…..\u001b[1G\u001b[J◇  \n\u001b[?25hMETA\nSEO Title: Senate Crypto Bill | Coinography August Vote Risk\nMeta Description: Follow the Senate crypto bill, the 60-vote hurdle, and the August timing risk shaping Bitcoin policy. Read the signals traders should watch.\nURL Slug: senate-crypto-bill-august-deadline-risk\nCategories: Regulation, Latest News\nPrimary Keyword: senate crypto bill\nSecondary Keywords: crypto market structure bill, Senate floor vote, Bitcoin commodity classification\n\n# Senate crypto bill faces 60-vote August deadline\n\nSenate crypto bill momentum is real, but the measure still faces a 60-vote Senate test and a narrow June to early August window. The committee step matters, yet it does not settle the harder issue, whether leaders can line up enough bipartisan support before recess cuts into floor time.\n\nThat is the number traders should keep centered. Republicans hold 53 seats, so at least seven Democrats are needed if the conference stays unified. Market reaction here is less about a near-term spike and more about shifting odds around timing, passage, and whether the summer window stays open.\n\nThis is not a policy breakout yet. It is a calendar trade.\n\n## Crypto market structure bill and Bitcoin commodity classification: What the senate crypto bill shows\n\nThe latest move was procedural, but still meaningful. [According to Cointelegraph](https://cointelegraph.com/news/senate-crypto-bill-august-advance-in-lame-duck-session-nydig?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound), the Senate Banking Committee advanced the bill after a delayed markup. That sends the crypto market structure bill toward the full chamber, while leaving the real whip count unresolved.\n\nThat framing lines up with [CoinDesk's recap](https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/05/17/the-clarity-act-took-a-step-forward-state-of-crypto), which treated the hearing as progress, not passage. The market takeaway is simple, Congress moved the file forward, but the path to law remains fragile and highly dependent on timing.\n\n[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]\n\n### June through early August is still the clean window\n\nNYDIG head of research Greg Cipolaro described the earlier July 4 target as more aspirational than fixed. His updated range, June through early August, is the more useful map because it tracks the last workable stretch before lawmakers leave and election politics start taking more oxygen.\n\nOnce the Senate moves deeper into late July, floor time gets tighter and leadership has less reason to force a divisive vote. At that point, a live summer catalyst can quickly turn into a lower-probability story.\n\n- Committee progress is done, but floor passage is not.\n- The 60-vote hurdle matters more than markup headlines.\n- Late-summer scheduling risk is now part of the trade.\n\n### A miss likely pushes the story into lame duck\n\nIf the bill does not clear in summer, the next likely opening is a lame-duck session after the election. That fallback is possible, but it is not guaranteed.\n\n\n[59 more lines in file. Use offset=41 to continue.][... 12340 more characters truncated]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779088011408}}
